Knights are easy. Far easier than I thought.

After finally ascending a priest a few weeks ago I started with a
knight. The game began quite promising with Gauntlets of Power on DL2
and an altar on DL4. After converting it and sacrificing for a while,
I got Grayswandir as the first present. As I prefer GS to the Foo
Brands, I decided to continue my exploration of the dungeon.

The Oracle level was a bonesfile which had a +3 robe for me. Near the
downstairs I accidentally displaced my pony onto a level teleporter so
I had to go on alone. I didn't even try to ride it, so it wasn't a big
issue. Sokoban had the bag. There was no interesting store on the
first levels so I could hardly identify any items. I decided to enter
the mines without poison resistance to get to the general store in
Minetown. On the way down I stepped on a trapdoor and found myself on
DL8. I was so worried about spiked pits that I searched for a few
turns before each move.

I managed to escape upstairs to Minetown and found a dog named Gaspode
attacking me. I tamed it and it helped to clear out most of the
stores. The bones didn't contain anything useful and after price-IDing
my stuff I returned to the main dungeon. I found some speed boots
lying around but still didn't manage to get poison resistance.

I found a jeweler's and almost emptied it with the help of my dog. I
dropped most rings into a sink and one of the was against
poison. Hmpf. At least I knew what ring I had to look for. On DL12 or
so I found a wand of polymorph and some polypiling gave me the desired
ring.

I stormed through the mines and stepped on a polymorph trap there. As
a queen bee I couldn't kill myself but at least I didn't lose any
armour. My dog killed all monsters before they could kill me so I had
to wait endlessly until the polymorph wore off. I grabbed the
luckstone and headed back up.

The game started to become a little difficult as I had neither magic
resistance nor reflection. When I came to the Medusa level I was glad
to see that there was no titan there. I crossed the water wearing a
ring of levitation and killed Medusa while blindfolded. Perseus'
statue at the shield of reflection in it, so this problem was
solved. I didn't dare to go to the castle yet, so I first took a look
at the Quest.

I lost my faithful dog to a jelly there, it seems that he didn't know
that acid can be rather unhealthy. Even without MR I decided to attack
Ixoth, after a few wizmode experiments showed me that I had a high
probability of success. I didn't even lose any armour during the short
fight and I got the MMoM.

On my way down to the castle I got a wish from a blessed smoky potion,
which gave me a +2 GDSM. I quickly cleared the castle and found the
wand at (0:1). I wished for a blessed spellbook of identify after I
figured out that I could cast it with about 30% success if I took of
my GoP. After recharging an other wish went for an amulet of
reflection so I could start two-weaponing with a silver sabre.

Gehennom was rather boring. All major demons died very quickly, only
Juiblex could have been a problem as my blessed unicorn horn didn't
cure my illness for three scary turns. How much time do you have
before you die of your illness? The Instadeath Spoiler says about 10
turns, but that seems a bit high to me.

A green slime death-dropped a magic marker so I could spare a wish on
that one. Some polypiling on Orcus' level completed my ascension
kit. When on DL45 I was surprised to hit the VS there, since the
castle was located rather deep (IIRC on DL28 or so). I entered the
Wizard's tower and notice that I forgot to bring a ring of conflict. I
must have accidentally polypiled it but a shop on Orcus' level had a
spare one.

After killing the Wizard I wanted to teleport to the VS level (via
confused controlled teleport) but I ended up on DL30 instead. A
subsequent try didn't help, too, so I rushed down the hard way. I met
Rodney somewhere but got rid of him quickly. Rodney reappeared in the
Sanctum but soon teleported to the temple. When I entered it, it
seemed to be that the two Wizards were attacking the Priest, even
though I was not using conflict at that time. Anyway, I killed all
three and got the Amulet.

On the way up, I noticed that I accidentally stashed my luckstone into
the BoH so I had to rebuild my luck. The mysterious force wasn't as
annoying as I expected. I made a short sacfest on my way up, but
unfortunately teleported away the Amulet of Yendor when a MMF was
created next to me. When I noticed that the MMF didn't have it in his
inventory after I killed him, I was getting a little nervous. But soon
I figured out that the Amulet must have been teleported away
independently of the MMF and must be lying around on the level
somewhere. I managed to find it and rushed further up. I picked up a
long sword and started dipping for Excalibur, since I couldn't think
of a knight ascending without having it. I got it at the second or
third fountain and reached the upstairs on DL1. I wanted to relearn
some spells, but the Wizard interrupted me.

I decided to go up anyways and was quite surprised that this time the
Wizard didn't leave behind a spellbook of dig (seems to be the case
when another Wizard is around). It didn't matter though as I had
enough wands of digging. On Air I was engulfed only once, conflict is
really handy there. On Water it took me ages to find the portal as it
was hidden by a object lying on it.

Astral was not a problem. First I tried the left altar, which was
guarded by Pestilence. Zapped him with a /oDeath and discovered that
the altar was the wrong one. On the return I got Sting from a player
monster. Next try was the middle one which turned out to be the right
altar.

My second back-to-back ascension!

